  "heading": "\\ring",
  "heading_latex": "\\textrm{ring}",
  "body_text": null,
  "page": null,
  "source": "[\\ring]\nDeclares: R ::= (X, +, *, 0, 1) is \\set via X\nspecifies:\n. + is \\(associative, commutative)::binary.operation:on{X}\n. * is \\(associative)::binary.operation:on{X}\n. 0 \"in\" X\n. 1 \"in\" X\nsatisfies:\n. [additive.identity]\n  forAll: x \"in\" X\n  then: x + 0 = x\n. [additive.inverse]\n  forAll: x \"in\" X\n  then:\n  . exists: y \"in\" X\n    suchThat: x + y = 0\n. [multiplicative.identity]\n  forAll: x \"in\" X\n  then:\n  . x * 1 = x\n  . 1 * x = x\n. [distributive]\n  forAll: a, b, c \"in\" X\n  then:\n  . a * (b + c) = (a * b) + (a * c)\n  . (a + b) * c = (a * c) + (b * c)\nEnables:\n. capability: x_ \"in\" R :<->: x_ is \\ring.element:of{R}\n  written: \"x_? \\in R?\"\nDocumented:\n. called: \"ring\"\n. description: \"A ring $(R, +, *, 0, 1)$ consists of an abelian addition group,\n                an associative multiplication with identity $1$, and two-sided\n                distributivity.\"\nId: \"5ca5fdca-692d-4f04-8420-aa01c909955d\"",
